course: dictionary
lesson: 8841
title: Shipwreck and shipwrecked
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A word can name a thing or event, which is a noun, or describe what happened, which is part of a verb. «Shipwreck» is a noun: it can mean the event when a ship is destroyed at sea, or the broken remains of that ship.
explain: «Paul travelled across the Roman world ... and was shipwrecked, beaten and put in prison.» The words beaten and prison show that Paul was going through hard times, so shipwrecked must be something bad that happened to his ship. It means his ship was wrecked.
explain: In «Gold never rusts, so a gold coin from a shipwreck still shines», the coin comes from a ship that sank long ago. Here shipwreck means the broken remains of that sunken ship. Try swapping in «a gold coin from a sunken ship» and the sentence still makes sense.
fact: «Shipwreck» can mean the event when a ship is destroyed or sinks at sea.
fact: «Shipwreck» can also mean the broken remains of a sunken ship.
fact: «Shipwrecked» means to be on a ship that is wrecked, often ending up on a shore or island.
fact: A shipwreck can be caused by a storm, by rocks, or by an accident.
fact: Divers study shipwrecks, such as the Titanic and the Mary Rose.
exercise: «Paul was shipwrecked, beaten and put in prison.» What does shipwrecked mean? | *His ship was wrecked at sea | He became a famous sailor who liked boats | He was given a prize for sailing | He went on a happy holiday
exercise: «Gold never rusts, so a gold coin from a shipwreck still shines.» In this sentence, what is a shipwreck? | A kind of fish that lives in the sea | A storm on the land | *The broken remains of a sunken ship | A rule about who gets help first
exercise: Which of these can cause a shipwreck? | A cake shaped like a boat | Learning to read a new book | A sunny afternoon at the park | *A storm at sea
test: What is a shipwreck when it means the event? | *A ship being destroyed or sinking at sea | A small boat used for fishing in a lake | A rocky island with a lighthouse | A race between two ships
test: The phrase «be shipwrecked» means: | *To be on a wrecked ship, often ending up on a shore or island | To build a new ship in a harbour | To swim across a wide lake | To sail very fast across the sea
exam: Which clue shows that shipwrecked is something bad? | starting churches | Paul travelled across the Roman world | yet he kept going | *beaten and put in prison
